He had lived in the house for three years, ever since Eleanor had found him as a shivering scrap of orange fur in a cardboard box outside the grocery store. He had grown into a sleek, muscular cat with a tail that flicked like a metronome when he was thinking. And lately, he had been thinking a great deal.

